 `finesPence`, `matchesBanned`, `standing`.
 
-`standing` is `suspended` when anything is being served, `warned` from 3 points, else `clear`.
+`standing` is `suspended` while any match is still outstanding as of `asOf`, `warned` from 3 points, else `clear`.
+
+### `GET /players/:playerId/suspensions?asOf=YYYY-MM-DD`
+`asOf` is required. Answers `playerId`, `asOf`, `matchesBanned`, `matchesServed`, `matchesOutstanding`, `suspended` and `entries`, oldest first.
+
+Each entry carries `cardId`, `fixtureId`, `teamId`, `shownOn`, `matches`, `served`, `outstanding`, `servedIn` (fixture ids in order) and `clearedOn` (the day the last match was served, else null).
+
+A card worth zero matches has no entry. A ban is served over played games of the team the card was shown for, one match per game off the earliest outstanding card for that side. Awarded, postponed and abandoned games serve nothing. Rescinded cards are excluded and any games they consumed fall through to later cards.
+
+### `GET /fixtures/:fixtureId/eligibility`
+Reads the day before the game and answers `fixtureId`, `playedOn`, `asOf` and `ineligible`: every registered player at either club with a match outstanding on `asOf`, home side first then by player id.
+
+Each entry carries `playerId`, `clubId`, `teamId` (their side in this game) and `outstanding`.
+
+While any match is outstanding the player is barred from every side of their current club. A transfer moves the bar, not the games already served.
 
